# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Person-level All of Us Controlled Tier data. These must never reach a public
# repository. They were untracked by care rather than by rule until 2026-09-02,
# which is one `git add results/` away from a disclosure.
#
# The rule for this repository: results/ holds aggregate model output --
# coefficients, standard errors, balance tables, counts -- and nothing with one
# row per participant. When adding a new output, ask which it is.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*/01_covid_cohort.csv
results/*/01b_phenotype_components_personlevel.csv
results/*/02_demographics.csv
results/*/03_charlson.csv
results/*/04_sdoh.csv
results/*/04b_sdoh_timing.csv
results/*/05_vaccination.csv
results/*/06_matching_variables.csv
results/*/07_matched_cohort.csv
results/*/08_regression_base.csv
results/*/09_sensitivity_flags.csv
results/*/*.rds
results/*/*.RData
results/*/*.fst

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-02: results/ is local-only by default.
#
# It held 81 aggregate files -- coefficient tables, balance tables, summary
# CSVs, figures -- on a PUBLIC repository, none of which had ever been screened
# against the All of Us rule on aggregate statistics covering fewer than 20
# participants. At least one was known to be at risk: the "never attended
# school" education stratum has under 20 participants, and the raw coefficient
# files carry no suppression where Table 2 does.
#
# The Data Availability statement promises *code*, not artifacts, so nothing we
# told readers depends on those files being here.
#
# 2026-09-04: three exceptions, screened and recorded in results/SCREENING.md --
# the values every figure draws, the figures themselves, and RUN.json. They are
# named below rather than force-added, so the screen is visible in the tree and
# a new file is not published by accident. Anything else added to results/ stays
# ignored until it is screened and named here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*
!results/figures/
!results/RUN.json
!results/SCREENING.md

# Word lock files
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-09-02: what is internal stays internal.
#
# The public surface of this repository is the numbered pipeline, the figure
# and check scripts, the README and the licence. Three directories are local
# only:
#
#   results/      model output; nothing person-level ever leaves the platform
#   submission/   the manuscript package, unpublished
#   archive/      project record, superseded code, and old drafts
#
# They are untracked, not deleted. Anything already in the history stays there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
submission/
archive/
working/
_to_delete/
__pycache__/
